(K-SADS), participated in a 2-week placebo-washout followed by an 8-week, randomized, double-blind, parallel-design, 
placebo-controlled trial of AMI, 5 mg/kg per day. The K-SADS nine-item scale, the Hamilton Depression Rating Scale, and 
the Clinical Global Impressions rating scale were used as outcome measures. RESULTS Thirty-one subjects were randomized 
(18 AMI, 13 placebo). Twenty-two subjects were study completers (12 AMI, 10 placebo). AMI's efficacy was suggested by 
