│ sample as a whole irrespective of treatment. Neither age nor sex were significantly related to improvement, except   │
│ on one behavioural measure where girls initially did better than boys. In addition, it was found that there was a    │
│ rapid relief of depression but neurotic symptomatology tended to persist.Cambridge University Press"},               │
│ {"study_index": 22, "title": "Meta‐analysis of early phase II studies with paroxetine in hospitalised depressed      │
│ patients", "abstract": "Five clinical trials compared the efficacy and tolerability of paroxetine (PRX) and          │
│ amitriptyline (AMT). A total of 70 depressed patients (aged 18–65 yrs) received treatment with PRX or AMT, after a   │
│ 1-wk placebo washout period. Efficacy was assessed with the Hamilton Rating Scale for Depression. A meta-analysis    │
│ was performed on all Ss. PRX, at a dose of 30 mg once daily, had antidepressant activity comparable to that of       │
│ conventional treatment with AMT 150 mg once daily. Adverse event profiles were similar in both treatments.(PsycINFO  │
│ Database Record (c) 2016 APA, all rights reserved)American Psychological Association"}, {"study_index": 23, "title": │
│ "Depression in children: relationship between plasma imipramine levels and response", "abstract": "The effects of    │
│ imipramine treatment and plasma drug levels were studied in 20 prepubertal children (16 males, 4 females; age range  │
│ 7-12 years) hospitalized for major depressive disorder (DSM-III criteria). No change in symptomatology was seen      │
│ after 2 weeks of individual/group/family psychotherapy, but 12 children experienced a remission within 6 weeks of    │
